territory implies mass, which means metal, which means more units.

time and construction power implies energy generation, which is managed through
an always open menu. Four buttons to determine how many of your engineers get
put toward energy exploitation. Sometimes you can find bonus chunks of energy
in the territory you find (hydrocarbon). This buffs the next energy building
you construct. They are naturally spread out and when losing territory, you lose
the energy that was built while that part of territory was controlled by your
guys.

mass comes with territory. Also you can assign energy and mass to improving it.
construction power costs energy and mass, depending on how your item is aligned -
for example, land tends to need 10 mass for every 1 energy, while air is the
opposite with 10 energy for every 1 mass. Naval needs 10 of both. High tech units
cost 100 of whichever, and experimental units cost 1000.

