some units are variants, and deserve separate pricing - for example, anti-air
units are land and can target air - therefore they should be 1 for 1, or 5 for 5
depending on how you want to think about it. Their costs should be equal. Most
units cost between 40 and 70 mass and 120 - 400 energy. they take construction
power, same as your engineers. Engineers can be assigned separately from your
builders. You can build more builders trivially, but engineers take time and
effort. If your air units have been overcome then enemy units can attack your
backline with plane attacks. If so, then you can lose engineers and builders
as your territory goes. If you lose 4% of your territory, then you lose 4% of
your engineers and builders. Random ones take damage, and they heal slowly. More
if there are many engineers. Build power can be used to create defenses which
deal damage to enemy units as they take your territory - for 1% of territory,
apply this much damage to the foe. In the full game we'll have many tower types
but for now treat them like artillery. They deal thorns damage, essentially. But
they lose in capacity as territory is claimed.

